-- title:
--   Germ reading j(qᵖ)-j(q)ᵖ at a supersingular crossing
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime with $5\le p$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. The symbol $\mathfrak X$ (`𝔛`) denotes a `DRModelPackage p`: a properness/flatness/integrality/normality package for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the level-$p$ Igusa scheme over $\mathbf Z$, together with curve models $M_0$ over $\mathbf Q$ and $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of the generic fibre, isomorphisms $e_0,e_\eta$ onto the corresponding base changes, Galois compatibility of the induced place dictionaries, the two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ and the smooth locus. Here `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of the level-$N$ modular function field inside Laurent series, and `chartAlgFin ℤ (modularFunctionFieldFull p) (jFull p)` is the integral closure of $\mathbf Z[j]$ in the level-$p$ modular function field (the finite $j$-chart algebra).
--
--   Generic-fibre chart normalisation. The open set $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the base change to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, pulled back from the image of the finite chart, is assumed nonempty, and `hMη` requires that for every $a$ in the finite $j$-chart algebra the germ of the corresponding section along that open set, read in the function field of $M_\eta$ and transported to `modularFunctionFieldBar p` by `𝔛.Mη.ffEquiv.symm`, has underlying Laurent series equal to `coeffEmb` applied to the Laurent series of $a$; that is, $e_\eta$ matches chart sections with the modular functions they name.
--
--   Level comparison. `ePl` is a bijection between the places of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` and those of `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, and `hePl_fun` requires that whenever $f$ and $f'$ in the two fields have the same underlying Laurent series, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $V$ if and only if $f'$ lies in that of $\mathrm{ePl}(V)$, and $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f = \mathrm{ePl}(V).\mathrm{evalAt}\,f'$.
--
--   Reduction and specialisation frame. $k$ is an algebraically closed perfect field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism; `data` is a `ModularPolynomialData p` (a monic $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(p)$ annihilating $(j,j_p)$) and `hKr` the Kronecker congruence, i.e. the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $p$ equals $(C(X)^p - X)(C(X) - X^p)$; `hα` and `hβ` assert integrality of the two level-raising maps at $(1,p)$; $P$ is a `PlaceSpecialization A p 1 data hKr k red hα hβ`, and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple P`. The accompanying hypotheses are: `hqN : ¬ p ∣ 1`; `hR : R.IsModel` (the two divisor laws together with the cusp laws at $\infty$ and at $0$); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces p 1 k` of supersingular places; `hreg : R.RegularityLaw W` and `hval : R.NodeValueLaw W`; a width function $e$ with `he` requiring $1 \le e(w)$ for $w \in W$; and `hVI`, requiring `R.ValueIntegralityLaw w` for every $w \in W$, i.e. that values at places above $w$ of elements of the node integers of $w$ lie in $A$.
--
--   The $\mathcal O$-frame. $O$ is a discrete valuation domain with an isomorphism `eO` onto the subring of the fixed field of the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` consisting of the elements lying in $A$, with `hϖO` saying that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$; $K$ is a fraction field of $O$ and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$ a ring homomorphism with `hιK` identifying $\iota_K$ on $O$ with the inclusion of `eO`, `hιA` saying the images of elements of $O$ lie in $A$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ with `htoκ` identifying $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ with $\mathrm{red}$ composed with that inclusion.
--
--   Resolved model and node. $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ is a `DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O k toκ` (a proper flat integral $O$-scheme $Y$ mapping properly to the base change of `DRModel p` along $\mathbf Z \to O$, regular of stalk Krull dimension at most two away from the $p$-invertible locus, isomorphic to the model over the smooth locus and over the generic fibre, with a finite node set carrying widths and an identification `nodeEquiv` of the nodes with the points of the intersection of the two components, together with its invertible component ideal sheaves); $\sigma_N$ is a bijection of $W$ with the node set and `hσN` requires $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(\sigma_N w) = e(w)$ for all $w$. A place $w \in W$ is fixed, together with a Boolean `swap`. In what follows $x_w$ denotes the point of the model over $O$ obtained from the node $\sigma_N\langle w, hw\rangle$ by `nodeEquiv`, the first projection of the pullback of `𝔛.compInf k` and `𝔛.compZero k`, the component map `𝔛.compInf k`, and the base change map along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$.
--
--   Orientation. `hswap` fixes the meaning of the bit: for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` fixed by the arithmetic Galois action of every element of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, and every section $s$ of the base change of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\mathbf Z \to O$ (that is, $s$ followed by the second projection is the identity) whose restriction along the composite $O \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$ into the generic fibre equals the $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-point of $\mathfrak X$ corresponding under `𝔛.Mη.pointEquivPlace` to the place $\mathrm{ePl}(V)$, pushed forward by $e_\eta$ and the first projection: if `P.IsStrictFst V` holds then the image of the closed point of $O$ under $s$ lies in the range of the base point map of `(if swap then 𝔛.compZero k else 𝔛.compInf k)` followed by the base change map along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$, and not in the range of the other component; and if `P.IsStrictSnd V` holds, the two components are interchanged. (Here `P.IsStrictFst V` asserts that the geometric Frobenius on places of level one sends $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$ to $P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,V$ while its square does not fix $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$, and `P.IsStrictSnd V` the mirror condition.)
--
--   The reading $\varphi$. The base change of `DRModel p` along $\mathbf Z \to O$ is assumed integral, and $\varphi$ is a ring homomorphism from its function field to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, pinned by two hypotheses: `hφO`, that for $a \in O$ the germ at $x_w$ of the global section coming from $a$ through the second projection has $\varphi$-image the image of $\iota_K(a)$ under $\overline{\mathbf Q} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`; and `hφj`, that for every $a$ in the finite $j$-chart algebra the $\varphi$-image of the germ of the corresponding chart section, read in the function field, has underlying Laurent series `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series of $a$ (the preimage open set in question being assumed nonempty).
--
--   Node point and $j$-pin. `hnodePt` requires that for every place $V$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V \in W$ which is fixed by the inertia action and satisfies neither `P.IsStrictFst V` nor `P.IsStrictSnd V`, every section $s$ as above with the same generic-fibre condition sends the closed point of $O$ to the crossing point attached to the node indexed by $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V$. `hxj` requires the existence of $\hat\jmath \in O$ whose reduction $\mathrm{red}(\iota_K \hat\jmath)$ equals $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen k 1`, and of an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $x_w$ with $\varphi$-image $j - \iota_K(\hat\jmath)$, where $j$ is `ProlongationTuple.jFun 1 p`.
--
--   Branches. Finally, `hspInf` and `hspZero` state that the images of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under `𝔛.compInf k` and under `𝔛.compZero k`, followed by the base change map along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$, both specialise to $x_w$.
--
--   Conclusion. The assertion is the conjunction of two implications, each producing an element $t_F$ of the stalk at $x_w$ of the base change of `DRModel p` along $\mathbf Z \to O$.
--
--   First: if $\mathrm{swap} = \mathrm{false}$, there is $t_F$ in that stalk such that $\varphi$ of the image of $t_F$ in the function field equals `ProlongationTuple.jQFun 1 p - ProlongationTuple.jFun 1 p ^ p`, that is $j(q^p) - j(q)^p$, and such that the image of $t_F$ under the specialisation map of stalks attached to `hspInf` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at the generic point of the $\infty$-component.
--
--   Second: if $\mathrm{swap} = \mathrm{true}$, there is $t_F$ in that stalk with the same identity $\varphi(t_F) = j(q^p) - j(q)^p$, whose image under the specialisation map attached to `hspZero` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at the generic point of the $0$-component.
--
--   This supplies the orientation datum at a supersingular crossing of the Deligne–Rapoport model in characteristic $p$: a germ at the crossing point whose function-field reading is $j(q^p) - j(q)^p$ and which vanishes along the branch selected by the orientation bit, the vanishing being expressed through the specialisation map from the stalk at the crossing point to the stalk at the generic point of that component. It feeds the node-coordinate and support description [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation_of_branch_of_jPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation_of_branch_of_jPin) and the width computation [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.width_eq_jWidth_of_exists_jFun_sub_mem_maximalIdeal_of_prolongationTuple`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.width_eq_jWidth_of_exists_jFun_sub_mem_maximalIdeal_of_prolongationTuple), where the widths of the nodes of the resolved model are matched with the depths read off from the $j$-line.
